1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,846
Resources are files and data that other AI apps can read from your site.

2
00:00:05,846 --> 00:00:10,630
This video shows what resources are, which types you can share, and how

3
00:00:10,630 --> 00:00:12,618
to add file, media, F.T.P.

4
00:00:12,618 --> 00:00:13,736
and S.F.T.P.

5
00:00:13,736 --> 00:00:14,730
resources.

6
00:00:19,330 --> 00:00:22,432
An AI app can only work from what it can see.

7
00:00:22,432 --> 00:00:26,872
Resources give it files and data to read, such as a policy document

8
00:00:26,872 --> 00:00:28,210
or a price list.

9
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:34,117
Without resources, people paste documents into a chat by hand, and the copy

10
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:35,900
soon goes out of date.

11
00:00:36,650 --> 00:00:40,157
With a resource, the app asks your site for the file when it

12
00:00:40,157 --> 00:00:43,080
needs it, so it always reads the current version.

13
00:00:43,830 --> 00:00:48,254
Resources are part of the Model Context Protocol server, so you manage them

14
00:00:48,254 --> 00:00:50,930
from the same menu as the server's prompts.

15
00:00:55,122 --> 00:00:59,838
Open Artificial Intelligence, Model Context Protocol, Resources.

16
00:00:59,838 --> 00:01:03,207
The list shows every resource with its type.

17
00:01:03,207 --> 00:01:04,892
Click Add Resource.

18
00:01:05,348 --> 00:01:08,633
Available Resource Types lists what you can share.

19
00:01:08,633 --> 00:01:14,088
File reads from the site's file providers, and Media shares files of the media library.

20
00:01:14,617 --> 00:01:19,831
FTP and FTPS, and SFTP, read files from a remote file server.

21
00:01:19,831 --> 00:01:23,877
They appear when their features are turned on.

22
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:29,351
The Recipe types share the site's recipes and their schemas with developer tools.

23
00:01:29,351 --> 00:01:32,234
You do not need them for everyday documents.

24
00:01:36,412 --> 00:01:37,869
Click Add on File.

25
00:01:37,869 --> 00:01:41,874
Enter a Display Text, which is the name you see in the list,

26
00:01:41,874 --> 00:01:45,272
and a Name, which identifies the resource to apps.

27
00:01:45,723 --> 00:01:48,935
Add a Description that says what the file holds.

28
00:01:48,935 --> 00:01:52,683
AI apps read it to decide whether the resource is useful.

29
00:01:53,140 --> 00:01:56,905
The MIME Type tells the app what kind of content it is.

30
00:01:56,905 --> 00:01:58,880
Plain text is the default.

31
00:01:59,334 --> 00:02:03,318
The Path points to the file, and the Full URI line shows the

32
00:02:03,318 --> 00:02:05,007
address that apps use.

33
00:02:05,007 --> 00:02:08,930
A placeholder in curly braces turns one resource into many:

34
00:02:08,930 --> 00:02:11,404
the app fills in the file it wants.

35
00:02:11,858 --> 00:02:12,966
Click Save.

36
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:15,768
The resource is listed with its type.

37
00:02:19,978 --> 00:02:23,878
A Media resource shares files of the media library.

38
00:02:23,878 --> 00:02:26,888
Click Add Resource, then Add on Media.

39
00:02:27,373 --> 00:02:29,250
Fill in the same fields.

40
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:34,194
In the Path, the placeholder path in curly braces stands for the location

41
00:02:34,194 --> 00:02:38,513
of a file in the media library, so an app can ask for any file.

42
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:44,143
To share a single file instead, replace the placeholder with its location.

43
00:02:44,143 --> 00:02:45,240
Click Save.

44
00:02:49,471 --> 00:02:53,826
SFTP and FTP resources read from a file server.

45
00:02:53,826 --> 00:02:59,990
Click Add Resource, then Add on SFTP, and give the resource a Display

46
00:02:59,990 --> 00:03:03,031
Text, a Name and a Description.

47
00:03:03,541 --> 00:03:09,561
Enter the Host, the Port, which is 22 by default, and the Username of the server.

48
00:03:10,017 --> 00:03:14,640
Sign in with a Password, or with a Private Key and its Passphrase.

49
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:18,107
Both are stored securely, and never shown again.

50
00:03:18,562 --> 00:03:23,687
The Proxy Settings, a Connection Timeout and a Keep-Alive Interval are optional, and

51
00:03:23,687 --> 00:03:26,192
help with firewalls and slow networks.

52
00:03:26,642 --> 00:03:27,906
Click Save.

53
00:03:27,906 --> 00:03:32,815
An FTP resource is added in the same way, with a Host, Port,

54
00:03:32,815 --> 00:03:36,681
Username and Password, and an Encryption Mode:

55
00:03:36,681 --> 00:03:40,102
None, Explicit, Implicit or Auto Detect.

56
00:03:40,569 --> 00:03:41,595
Click Save.

57
00:03:41,595 --> 00:03:45,939
The site only stores the settings, so try each resource from an AI

58
00:03:45,939 --> 00:03:47,869
app before you rely on it.

59
00:03:52,069 --> 00:03:54,086
Policies and price lists:

60
00:03:54,086 --> 00:03:59,679
publish the document once, and every connected AI app reads the current version.

61
00:04:00,429 --> 00:04:02,417
Files on a partner's server:

62
00:04:02,417 --> 00:04:04,112
read them over S.F.T.P.

63
00:04:04,112 --> 00:04:06,449
without copying them to your site.

64
00:04:07,199 --> 00:04:08,883
Media library documents:

65
00:04:08,883 --> 00:04:13,149
share brochures and manuals that your editors already keep up to date.

66
00:04:13,899 --> 00:04:15,360
Share with care:

67
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:20,669
an app can read whatever a resource points to, so choose paths on purpose.

68
00:04:22,669 --> 00:04:26,196
Add a resource for each file or data set you want AI apps

69
00:04:26,196 --> 00:04:29,274
to read, and they always see the current version.

70
00:04:29,274 --> 00:04:30,729
Thanks for watching.

